{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in","id":1488006,"title":"The Year TC: Aegis will take place in.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aegis"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-26T05:16:12-07:00","id":1488006,"title":"The Year TC: Aegis will take place in.","content":"Very curious when in the Bronze Age, Trinity Continuum: Aegis will be set, as it will definitely inform the type of cultures and adventures the player characters will get involved in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T12:49:23-07:00","id":1488077,"title":"","content":"I don't know, but the traditional date of the Trojan War is around 1200BCE. From 1500BCE ( before Perseus) to about 100CE would suit me. But if a long time period is out, nearer the date of the fall of Troy is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T22:18:32-07:00","id":1488320,"title":"","content":"If they set it in the actual Bronze Age they\u2019ve got the issue of historic Mycenaean civilization vs the Greece of the legends of Classical Greece (which tend to look like Classical Greece but with demigods and monsters). It\u2019s not unlike the question rpgs run into trying to plant Arthurian myth in a particular era (what Pendragon I believe goes with is that Camelot is a utopian anachronism that does become very like the romanticized high Middle Ages in terms of culture and technology, and society collapses back to the norms of the 6th century with its fall).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T01:56:05-07:00","id":1488339,"title":"","content":"Well the collapse of Bronze Age societies around the eastern Mediterranean and the traditional date for the fall of Troy come suspiciously close. <br /> <br /> Alien interference to prevent a competitor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T18:37:54-07:00","id":1488518,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Let's say sometime in the later half of the 13th century BC. This would be the ancient Bronze Age Greek Aegean culture and the near end of the Minoan civilization in Crete. <br /> <br /> This would also be the period of the New Kingdom period of Egypt, which at the time was an empire holding territory in the Levant and Nubia. This may or may not also correspond with the period of Jacob in the book of Genesis, depending on what sources/interpretations you prefer. <br /> <br /> You've also got the Hittite Empire in Turkey and Mesopotamia. (There's apparently some speculation that the Trojans are part of the Hittites. This is, IIRC, the interpretation Eric Shanower used in his Age of Bronze graphic novels.) And the Phoenician city states in modern day Lebanon. <br /> <br /> I think you've also got the end of the Indus Valley civilization and the early Vedic civilization in northwest India and the Shang in northeastern China. <br /> <br /> The setting may also include stuff from from Greek mythology like Aethiopia, Hyperborea, the Amazons, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T08:15:00-07:00","id":1488567,"title":"","content":"As <b>No one of Consequence </b> (the man is indispensable) brought up the Indus River civilization let's remember that, other than we know they worshipped a figure that seems to be Shiva or a precursor to that deity, they're pretty much a total blank to the modern world. They could be Atlantis, a victim of aliens, or whatever fits your game. I personally suggest a source of unsolvable mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T10:24:59-07:00","id":1488581,"title":"","content":"I'm curious as to whether Aegis will use the Talent/Mesmerist/Stalwart rules from Adventure! with new splat names, or if it'll go with a different twist like in Aether. While a Bronze Age campaign would put the setting well before the Doyen dropped a suppression effect over the planet in 1922, the setting is <i>well before</i> that era; 3,000+ years is enough of a gap that I could easily accept the player characters being on par with Adventure! era characters despite the lack of Doyen interference, since 120+ generations is plenty of time for humanity's latent potential to significantly improve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T11:17:39-07:00","id":1488584,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that \u00c6gis ends up using something a bit more high-powered than that. It's supposed to be about Heroes, Magicians, and Gods, after all. <br /> <br /> Well, not <i>literally</i>; and I don't want the Superhumans of \u00c6gis to be on par with the Gods of Scion. But I'd rather they be closer to Nova-level than Stalwart-level. <br /> <br /> I'd like the Magicians to be roughly on par with Psions, though not necessarily using the Aptitudes of the \u00c6on era. <br /> <br /> And I'd like the Heroes to have access to Masteries the way Assassins do, but without the whole \u201chiding in the Shadow\u201d thing. Basically, use Masteries to make them roughly on par with Terrestrial Exalted (though without the whole Elemental theme). <br /> <br /> In fact, Masteries might be a better baseline to work from if they end up using a variant of Talents for everything, the way they've done in Adventure! and \u00c6ther.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T11:45:26-07:00","id":1488589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in?p=1488584#post1488584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that \u00c6gis ends up using something a bit more high-powered than that. It's supposed to be about Heroes, Magicians, and Gods, after all.<br /> <br /> Well, not <i>literally</i>; and I don't want the Superhumans of \u00c6gis to be on par with the Gods of Scion. But I'd rather they be closer to Nova-level than Stalwart-level.<br /> <br /> I'd like the Magicians to be roughly on par with Psions, though not necessarily using the Aptitudes of the \u00c6on era.<br /> <br /> And I'd like the Heroes to have access to Masteries the way Assassins do, but without the whole \u201chiding in the Shadow\u201d thing. Basically, use Masteries to make them roughly on par with Terrestrial Exalted (though without the whole Elemental theme).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easy to seem godlike when common soldiers are wielding bronze age weapons: <a href=\"https://www.history.com/news/bronze-age-weapons\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.history.com/news/bronze-age-weapons</a><br /> <br /> A combat focused stalwart who maxes out should be able to go through trivial opponents like a scythe through wheat.<br /> <br /> Do also note that Novas are an unnatural phenomenon. Divis Mal's work super saturated the world with an abnormal amount of quantum energy, creating novas who were bloated on way more energy than they were equipped to handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T12:10:35-07:00","id":1488592,"title":"","content":"<i>Anyone</i> can go through trivial opponents like a scythe through wheat. That's what \u201ctrivial\u201d <i>means</i>. <br /> <br /> And I'm not sure that Novas <i>are</i> an unnatural phenomenon. I think they're what happens <i>naturally</i> when you have that much Quantum energy in the environment. Stalwarts and Superiors are what you get when the Quantum is artificially <i>suppressed</i> (by the Doyen shield in the first case, and by the Nakamura process in the second), and \u00c6on-era Aberrants are what you get when there just isn't as much Quantum available. <br /> <br /> My point is that I'd prefer to have \u00c6gis operate on a higher power level than Adventure!, instead of being \u201cAdventure!, but in ancient Greece\u201d. If you need justification for it, it could be some combination of their not being a doyan shield to suppress the effect, and the effect being a lot more localized and thus concentrated: just Greece, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-31-2022, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T07:42:10-07:00","id":1489229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in?p=1488592#post1488592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Anyone</i> can go through trivial opponents like a scythe through wheat. That's what \u201ctrivial\u201d <i>means</i>. <br /> <br /> And I'm not sure that Novas <i>are</i> an unnatural phenomenon. I think they're what happens <i>naturally</i> when you have that much Quantum energy in the environment. Stalwarts and Superiors are what you get when the Quantum is artificially <i>suppressed</i> (by the Doyen shield in the first case, and by the Nakamura process in the second), and \u00c6on-era Aberrants are what you get when there just isn't as much Quantum available. <br /> <br /> My point is that I'd prefer to have \u00c6gis operate on a higher power level than Adventure!, instead of being \u201cAdventure!, but in ancient Greece\u201d. If you need justification for it, it could be some combination of their not being a doyan shield to suppress the effect, and the effect being a lot more localized and thus concentrated: just Greece, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the addition of magogs and mystical focus tools in Aether, I suspect that is how they will be doing character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27511-fanggrip","name":"FangGrip","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T20:17:50-07:00","id":1489448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in?p=1488584#post1488584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that \u00c6gis ends up using something a bit more high-powered than that. It's supposed to be about Heroes, Magicians, and Gods, after all.<br /> <br /> Well, not <i>literally</i>; and I don't want the Superhumans of \u00c6gis to be on par with the Gods of Scion. But I'd rather they be closer to Nova-level than Stalwart-level.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're worried about the Talent system not being enough to model god-like beings, that may not be a concern. Having just finished the Gifts chapter of the Aether Kickstarter manuscript, it looks like Magogs are using the Talent system to potentially hit Scale 4 in various physical, mental, and social tasks right out of character creation, and can reach scale 6 with as little as 20 xp. If the affects of Gifts that boost scale stack, a Magog with Intuitive Facet 5, two purchases of Paragon (Cunning or Dexterity), and one purchase of Rapidity of Flesh can wind up hitting speed scale 8. Throw in the Swift Edge and they're speed scale 9. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T21:33:17-07:00","id":1490096,"title":"","content":"Point connected to <b>TC Aegis </b>era time and place - <b>We are constantly reminded by TC devs that 'AEON exists in every era, in one way or another'</b>. I wonder if in <b>Aegis</b> it will be some Temple ( Temple of Aeons) or maybe Prophecy/Main Quest ( Prophecy of Aeons)? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> The <u><i>bad</i></u> example for doing this kind of thing is <b>Assassin's Creed</b> series - lore of game said that 'Assassins existed always' - we also got lore that first Hidden Blade was used in 465 BCE on Xerxes of Persia as first real tyrant. However, by developments and marketing reason, <b>AC Origin</b> the retconed 13 years of lore that Assassins Order was created in 48 BCE with help of Cleopatra. \ud83d\ude1e And in next game <b>AC Odyssey</b> we practically already HAVE Assassins Order in 430 BCE Greece. \ud83d\ude22<br /> <br /> I love <b>AC</b> series my whole gamer heart - but I still have a big problem with internal inconsistently about it. <u><i>Do not make this mistake for <b>T</b><b>rinity</b></i></u>. Give us AEON in <b>Aegis</b> era also! \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2022, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T01:43:48-07:00","id":1490105,"title":"","content":"If I were to make a guess - with the caveat that I know nothing about \u00c6gis's planned themes and whatnot - I would presume the following possibilities for Societies:<ul><li>The period version of the \u00c6on society, maybe as a mystery cult akin to those of the Pythagoreans or the Oracles</li> <li>Some sort of monster hunter group</li> <li>The new gods who want to overthrow the current gods the way they did the Titans</li> <li>Super scientists and inventors akin to Daedalus and Archimedes</li> <li>A chthonic mystery cult</li> <li>Some sort of group claiming to be the inheritors of lost Atlantis</li> <li>The Amazons</li> <li>Explorers who routinely go off to \u00c6thiopia, Hyperboria, and other unusual places</li> </ul>That is just off the top of my head. I'm sure \u00c6gis will end up having a bunch of out of left field ideas, the same way \u00c6ther does, which would add to, alter, invalidate, spin, fold, or mutilate any of the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T05:22:37-07:00","id":1490373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in?p=1490096#post1490096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point connected to <b>TC Aegis </b>era time and place - <b>We are constantly reminded by TC devs that 'AEON exists in every era, in one way or another'</b>. I wonder if in <b>Aegis</b> it will be some Temple ( Temple of Aeons) or maybe Prophecy/Main Quest ( Prophecy of Aeons)? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping with the Esoteric Order of the Aeons, they'd hint that they were much older than they appeared (ala Hickman's Brotherhood of the Shield as a precursor to Marvel's SHIELD), but alas that wasn't to be. Mostly because I am hoping for some sort of Rennisaince era book and the Brotherhood would rock then.<br /> <br /> I'd personally like a group that has a link to the modern Aeon Society, perhaps the result of Mercer being unstuck in time. Perhaps the Temple of the Aeons was formed by someone who had a &quot;vision&quot; of the future and built the Temple in veneration of the strange wonders he saw from the Realm of the Gods.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T05:37:35-07:00","id":1490376,"title":"","content":"We know from <b>Assassins</b> that there was an organization in antiquity that collected dangerous artifacts (the Order of Leonidas entry). My guess is that would've been the Aeon equivalent, considering the current Babel Dossier and such. Who knows.<br /> <br /> Seeing how they went into a completely different direction than I expected with Aether, I'm happily looking forward to the cool things they'll do with Aegis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","user":"NullApostle","date":". 08-16-2022, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:13:32-07:00","id":1490387,"title":"","content":"I'm a big ( literally and metaphorically ) <b>Assassin's Creed </b>fan. Right now I play <b>AC Origins</b>, that is set in Roman protected Cleopatra's Egipt, circa 48 BCE. And I REALLY get itch on Ancient Trinity - Aegis, as it suppose - right now.<br /> <br /> ESPECIALLY, as I got 'future sword from space', cause AC devs given you crossover event with <b>Final Fantasy XV</b>. \ud83d\ude2e It looks EXATLCY like how various Trinity Eras are interacting with past of previous ones, on Continuum!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LfAEuKQXYV4\" data-code=\"LfAEuKQXYV4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LfAEuKQXYV4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T18:43:09-07:00","id":1490666,"title":"","content":"While every era has something equivalent to \u00c6on, from Adventure! onwards it's the first time it's a continuous organization lasting through multiple eras. That's one of the things that makes it special.<br /> <br /> I don't currently have any plans for any other \u00c6on-equivalents lasting through multiple successive time periods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T02:04:52-07:00","id":1490687,"title":"","content":"Afterall, it's Trinity Continuum, not \u00c6on Continuum.<br /> <br /> Back to original theme, I think its perfectly fine to use a generic &quot;Greece during Bronze Age&quot; as the numbers we use now for the years are not used at the time, and Greece is big enough to have something happening in one side without affecting the other for at least a few years.<br /> <br /> I would love to have Troy War as one of the different sub-settings, as well as to see some monsters around (quantum or aether powered).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T04:02:49-07:00","id":1490694,"title":"","content":"I still stick with Prophecy of Aeons for my own games - maybe just as story seed then.<br /> <br /> What would mean &quot;Greece during Bronze Age&quot; in terms of years? <br /> <br /> Wikipedia points Greece Bronze Age as circa 3300 \u2014 1100 BC - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aegean_civilization?wprov=sfla1\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aegean...on?wprov=sfla1</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T15:55:20-07:00","id":1490744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in?p=1490694#post1490694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would mean &quot;Greece during Bronze Age&quot; in terms of years?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fifth post in this thread gave a well reasoned prediction for when it could take place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T23:56:43-07:00","id":1490767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in?p=1488518#post1488518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've also got the Hittite Empire in Turkey and Mesopotamia. (There's apparently some speculation that the Trojans are part of the Hittites. This is, IIRC, the interpretation Eric Shanower used in his Age of Bronze graphic novels.) And the Phoenician city states in modern day Lebanon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for recommendation for <b>Age of Bronze</b> graphics novels - will read them in the waiting for <b>TC Aegis</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T00:46:01-07:00","id":1490769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in?p=1490767#post1490767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for recommendation for <b>Age of Bronze</b> graphics novels - will read them in the waiting for <b>TC Aegis</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They are really good, but I don't hold out much hope for it ever being finished. At this point, he's been at it for over twenty years and is only to the very early part of the war. At this rate, I will probably be dead before he gets to Hector vs Achilles or the Trojan Horse. \u2639\ufe0f","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T17:30:21-08:00","id":1500795,"title":"","content":"I think that given the simple fact that <b>Aether</b>, <b>Anima</b>, <b>Aeon</b>, <b>Adventure!</b>, and <b>Aberrant</b>, all involve either alien interference with the Earth or a reaction to alien interference, I assume that <b>Aegis </b>will also involve alien interference with Earth.<br /> <br /> This setting's equivalent of Typhon, the Titans, and the Telchines (the gods of ancient Rhodes, they raised Poseidon, and later fought the Olympians) are likely to be aliens. If it's Gods equal Novas, Magicians equal psiads, and Heroes equal Talents, aliens take a four place.<br /> <br /> Further fun, human population on Earth doesn't reach fifty million until 1000BCE. That equals a lot of wilderness to hide aliens in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-20-2023, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T19:21:54-08:00","id":1500895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in?p=1500795#post1500795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further fun, human population on Earth doesn't reach fifty million until 1000BCE. That equals a lot of wilderness to hide aliens in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just aliens. It is canon to the setting that Strange Places become less common as the world becomes more thoroughly explored. With the low population density and limited travel of the bronze age, there should be a lot of Strange Places even with the likely limited geographical area of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T21:09:24-08:00","id":1500897,"title":"","content":"Perhaps; perhaps not. There's reason to think that most Strange Places might have originated during TC:\u00c6ther as part of the alien incursion that was responsible for that era. It's possible that the \u201cmeteorite\u201d responsible for TC:\u00c6gis might <i>also</i> have created some Strange Places; but it's far from certain. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T05:01:21-08:00","id":1500918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1488006-the-year-tc-aegis-will-take-place-in?p=1500897#post1500897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps; perhaps not. There's reason to think that most Strange Places might have originated during TC:\u00c6ther as part of the alien incursion that was responsible for that era. It's possible that the \u201cmeteorite\u201d responsible for TC:\u00c6gis might <i>also</i> have created some Strange Places; but it's far from certain.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do we know that a meteorite is responsible for TC Aegis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T06:06:10-08:00","id":1500923,"title":"","content":"Maybe not a meteorite (which is why I had that in quotes); but we do know that something from the sky crashed into Mount Olympus, and that this was TC:\u00c6gis's counterpart to the Hammersmith Event. This was mentioned in a recent Onyx Path podcast where the developers of TC:\u00c6gis were being interviewed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T09:11:47-08:00","id":1500942,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly just looking forward to the legendary hissy fits whenever two novas called Zeus meet.<br /> <br /> But yeah, even if aliens were responsible for the \u00c6gis era, it's probably more 'a quantum warp ship crashed into the big hill' than 'aliens were the titans'. If anything I expect some kind of 'this period is actually poorly remembered' deal, where the myths of the Titanomachy spring from 'big boom and then gods appear, obviously the result of a divine war'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}